 \"real, credible, and charismatic in the same way he was perceived by his contemporaries\". Chernow, a former business journalist, was inspired to write the book while researching another biography on Washington's long-time aide Alexander Hamilton. Washington: A Life took six years to complete and makes extensive use of archival evidence. The book was released to wide acclaim from critics, several of whom called it the best biography of Washington ever written. In 2011, the book won the Pulitzer Prize for Biography or Autobiography, as well as the New-York Historical Society's American History Book Prize.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington%3A_A_Life","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"Washington: A Life","author":"Ron Chernow","publisher":"Penguin Press","publicationDate":"October 5, 2010","publicationPlace":"United States","pages":"904 (hardcover)","isbn":"978-1-59420-266-7","language":"English","subject":"George Washington","genre":"Non-fiction; biography"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-washington-a-life-ron-chernow"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-latimes-history-wikipedia-los-angeles-times-book-prize-for-history","label":"Wikipedia: Los Angeles Times Book Prize for History","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Times_Book_Prize_for_History","accessedAt":"2026-08-01T20:39:08.468Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/books"},{"id":"source-award-record-ny-history-american-history-wikipedia-new-york-historical-book-prizes","label":"Wikipedia: New York Historical book prizes","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Historical_book_prizes#Barbara_and_David_Zalaznick_Book_Prize_in_American_History","accessedAt":"2026-08-01T20:39:08.468Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","